{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["And He said <b>that are in the waters beneath the earth</b> to include the demons — 'beneath the waters and their inhabitants' (Job 26:5). Thus the Sages said (Mekhilta, here): to include the *buvya*. And concerning all of them He said <b>you shall not bow down to them nor serve them</b> — by any form of worship at all, even if his intention is not to withdraw himself from the domain of HaKadosh Barukh Hu. And behold, He voided all forms of worship in their entirety for the sake of the Name that is singular, may He be exalted (Sanhedrin 60a)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The term בוביא (buvya) is left transliterated; it appears to refer to a type of aquatic creature or demon mentioned in the Mekhilta. The phrase 'לשם המיוחד ית״ב' uses the abbreviation ית׳ for 'may He be exalted,' resolved here as 'may He be exalted.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:11:10.949227907Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}